{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): In you come, Liam. Mum and Dad can both sit. I'll grab a few numbers once the doctor's said hello.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): G'day. What's been happening with him?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's crook, doctor. Fever and a cough, and with his asthma I'm a bit spun out, to be honest.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): When did the fever start?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Three days. Wednesday arvo, after kinder.",
  "[SEG0006] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Nah, it was Saturday. He's been hot since Saturday, that's five days.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Saturday he was just worn out from kinder, that wasn't a fever. The fever's three days.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Alright. Mum's saying three days, you're saying five, so roughly three to five days and we can't lock it. How high has it been at home?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): This morning it was 38.9.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Last night the thermometer said 40. I watched it climb.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): You pulled it out early. When it actually beeped it was 39.4, I've got the photo. This morning was 38.9.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Yeah alright, 39.4. Still rotten.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): So a peak of 39.4 last night and 38.9 this morning. What have you given him?",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Strawberry Panadol, the pink syrup. One 5 mil spoon, four times a day.",
  "[SEG0015] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I gave two spoons. One looked tiny.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): It's one 5 mil spoon, not two. And be honest, did you give him the orange bottle?",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Yeah, the orange Nurofen, this morning. About a spoon, maybe a bit under. I sort of tipped it, I didn't measure.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me play that back. Pink Panadol through the day, and you two don't agree if it was one 5 ml spoon or two. And one rough spoon of orange Nurofen this morning. Any medicine allergies?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No. Nothing.",
  "[SEG0020] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Penicillin. He came up in a rash as a bub and we were told to steer clear.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): That GP reckoned it was the virus, not a real allergy. I don't count it.",
  "[SEG0022] person_5 (PATIENT): My throat hurts. Are you gonna jab me?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sore throat, I've got that, and no jab from me yet. Any vomiting, any rash today, ears sore?",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No spew, no rash, he's not pulling at his ears. He won't eat, and the cough's rotten at night.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): On what I've heard so far I'd keep him at home, push fluids, Panadol at the labelled dose, and I wouldn't order a chest picture.",
  "[SEG0026] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Hang on though, he's been breathing really fast. The purple puffer, Seretide, two puffs morning and night, and the blue Ventolin every couple of hours yesterday.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (NURSE): Sorry to jump in. Obs just now, temp 38.6, pulse 126, respirations 32, oxygen sat 94 percent on air.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right, that changes things. With him breathing that fast and sats of 94 I'm not leaving the x-ray. We'll do a chest x-ray today.",
  "[SEG0029] person_5 (PATIENT): Will the picture hurt? Can I go home?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): It won't hurt, mate, and you go home after, not into a bed. Mum, the asthma, since when?",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Since he was three. Is it pneumonia? Does he need antibiotics? Do I stop the Nurofen? What if the x-ray's normal? Can he go to kinder Monday? Sorry, I just...",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Pneumonia's possible. I can't call it until the film's back, so it's not a diagnosis, and no antibiotics from me today. Use one 5 ml spoon of the Panadol, not two, and leave the Nurofen unless we say otherwise. Kinder waits until the fever's gone.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (NURSE): I can slot the chest x-ray in down the hall straight after, if you want it now.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Yes, book it for today. If the film doesn't explain it we might add a blood test, but only if we need to. I want him seen back here tomorrow morning, not next week.",
  "[SEG0035] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Is the Saturday clinic actually on?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (DOCTOR): Morning clinic, yes. If he's struggling to breathe overnight, or he stops drinking, don't wait for us, go to emergency. Liam, Mum stays with you the whole time.",
  "[SEG0037] person_5 (PATIENT): I want Mum. Is it bad?",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I've got you, darling. X-ray now, one spoon, back tomorrow. Thank you."
 ],
